      "id": "5pxw0gh",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Background of Indian National Movement"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Indian National Movement unfolded through critical stages starting with the Formation of Indian National Congress (INC).",
        "Early leadership transition moved from the Moderate Phase (1885–1905) to the Extremist Phase (1905–1919).",
        "Mass mobilizations included the Swadeshi Movement, Home Rule Movement (1916), and Non-Cooperation Movement (1920–1922).",
        "The Gandhian Phase spearheaded pivotal nationwide campaigns such as the Civil Disobedience Movement (1930–1934) and the Quit India Movement (1942), culminating in the Independence of India."
      ],
      "id": "28r3nyf"
    },
